Data provenance refers to tracking the origin and history of input data through metadata and digital watermarking techniques. Provenance data tracking processes can include and assist AI Actors across the lifecycle who may not have full visibility or control over the various trade-offs and cascading impacts of early-stage model decisions on downstream performance and synthetic outputs. For example, by selecting a watermarking model to prioritize robustness (the durability of a watermark), an AI actor may inadvertently diminish computational complexity ( the resources required to implement watermarking). Organizational risk management efforts for enhancing content provenance include:

• Tracking provenance of training data and metadata for GAI systems;

• Documenting provenance data limitations within GAI systems;
